#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-7-model-options.ipynb:93
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we add a thermal model to the SPMe. From the "
"`documentation <https://docs.pybamm.org/en/latest/source/api/models/"
"base_models/base_battery_model.html>`__, we see that we have a choice of "
"various thermal models. For a deeper look at the thermal models see the "
"`thermal models notebook <../models/thermal-models.ipynb>`__. We choose the "
"lumped thermal model, which solves the spatially-dependent heat equation on "
"our battery geometry, and couples the temperature with the electrochemistry. "
"We set the model options by creating a Python dictionary:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-7-model-options.ipynb:-1
msgid "[2]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-7-model-options.ipynb:-1
msgid "options = {\"thermal\": \"lumped\"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-7-model-options.ipynb:115
msgid ""
"and passing it to the model. Then, the model can be solved as shown in "
"previous notebooks. We also increase the current to amplify the thermal "
"effects:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-7-model-options.ipynb:-1
msgid "[3]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-7-model-options.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"model = pybamm.lithium_ion.SPMe(options=options)  # loading in options\n"
"\n"
"sim = pybamm.Simulation(model)\n"
"sim.solve([0, 3600])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-7-model-options.ipynb:140
msgid ""
